An example case in ecology can be simulated here. You as a researcher are tracking the movement and survival of a population of animals using GPS telemetry.
Your research question is: Are faster animals less vulnerbale to predators?
You noticed after running a linear model (lm(risk ~ speed, data = data)), a negative relationship between how fast the animal moves (movement speed), and how long it survived.
However, you are a well knowledgeable biologist and you know body size also affects movement speed. The larger the animal, the slower it is relative to a smaller animal. But also, larger animals can defend themselves from an attack than a small individual. When controlling for body mass in your model (lm(risk ~ speed + mass, data = data)), you see that the relationship is gone.
